# Build context for `docker build -f apps/backend/Dockerfile .` (repo root).
# Keeps secrets and build artifacts out of the image and shrinks context
# upload. The Dockerfile only COPYs apps/backend/, VERSION, and
# packages/donation-dialog/package.json, so this mainly guards against
# accidentally baking apps/backend/.env or a stale `backend` binary in.

# Node / build artifacts
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.cache

# Local env (never bake secrets into the image)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Go build artifacts
apps/backend/backend
**/*.exe

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.git
.gitignore
